cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Merlin in your research, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "Merlin: polynomial-time quantum simulator for non-Clifford quantum error correction"
abstract: >-
  Merlin (merlin-sim) is a polynomial-time quantum simulator for non-Clifford
  quantum error correction circuits. It simulates magic state distillation,
  magic state cultivation and code switching protocols built from CNOT, T and
  Pauli gates, Z measurements and compatible X measurements, by tracking
  third-order phase-polynomial states.
